<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<wintakPluginPackage>
  <metadata>
    <!-- C-17: this package previously declared <id>FeatureLink</id> and <version>2.6.9</version>,
         BYTE-IDENTICAL to WinTAK5.6/MANIFEST.xml, while containing a materially different and
         REGRESSED binary. Two different plugins with the same identity are indistinguishable to
         the plugin manager and to any support engineer reading a manifest, so a 5.7 build could
         silently masquerade as (or displace) a 5.6 one. Both fields are now distinct.

         The version is deliberately NOT 2.7.0: this tree is not at parity with 5.6 and must not
         claim to be. "0.9.0-pre" says what it is. See
         docs/remediation/wp3-wintak-57-parity.md for the file-by-file gap list.

         DO NOT SHIP THIS PACKAGE. It is missing Mission Package layer share, send-item-to-PLI,
         live marker visibility, the orphan-marker sweep, display-style resolution, and every fix
         applied to 5.6 during the audit remediation. -->
    <id>FeatureLink.WinTAK57</id>
    <version>0.9.0-pre</version>
    <sdkVersion>5.7.0.144</sdkVersion>
    <takVariants>
    </takVariants>
    <description>FeatureLink (WinTAK 5.7 PORT — INCOMPLETE, NOT FOR RELEASE): browse and sync ArcGIS Feature Layers to the map, and send this device's Position Location Information (PLI) to an ArcGIS Feature Layer via OAuth2 sign-in. This 5.7 tree is a stale fork of an older 5.6 and is missing layer share, send-item-to-PLI, live marker visibility, orphan-marker cleanup and display-style resolution. Use the WinTAK 5.6 package unless you are specifically testing the 5.7 port.</description>
